      en: "Ha Long is the capital city of Quang Ninh Province and the primary gateway to the renowned Ha Long Bay in northeastern Vietnam. The bay features an expansive landscape of approximately 1,600 limestone islands and islets, formed over 500 million years of geological activity and erosion. Historically, the area was a site of significant naval battles against invading forces, and its name, which translates to \"Descending Dragon,\" originates from local folklore. The city itself has seen rapid transformation from a coal-mining hub into a modern service and tourism center, supported by the development of the Bai Chay and Hon Gai districts. In 1994, UNESCO designated Ha Long Bay as a World Heritage Site for its exceptional aesthetic value and geological importance, followed by a second recognition for its geomorphology in 2000. Large-scale infrastructure projects have integrated the region into the global transport network, facilitating maritime trade.",
